{"name":"Crossbow","hex":"#60543f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crossbow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mechanised weapon, based on the bow and arrow, that shoots bolts.","A portable ballista that can be held in the hand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crossbow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crossbow","blocks":[{"text":"A crossbow is a ranged weapon using an elastic launching device consisting of a bow-like assembly called a prod, mounted horizontally on a main frame called a tiller, which is hand-held in a similar fashion to the stock of a long gun. Crossbows shoot arrow-like projectiles called bolts or quarrels. A person who uses a crossbow is called a crossbowman, an arbalister or an arbalist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg/330px-Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossbow","wikidata":"Q181947"},{"title":"Crossbow (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Crossbow is a 1987 historical drama action-adventure television series that aired on CBN Cable Network. The series was produced by Steven North and Richard Schlesinger for Robert Halmi Inc., in co-production with French television network FR3. It was filmed entirely on location in France, mostly in the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region, in the Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur region, and in the Occitania region (Villeneuve-lès-Avignon)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Crossbow_tv_series_titlecard.jpg/330px-Crossbow_tv_series_titlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossbow_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q651567"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Han_crossbow_trigger_mechanism.jpg/500px-Han_crossbow_trigger_mechanism.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai